WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
Hi, guys. Welcome back to our
Business English series.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.840
Let's jump straight back in with the 
rest of our tips for improving delegation.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:12.810
Trust your team. Now, I
know some of you are screaming

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:17.100
at me through the screen right
now, 'but they need to earn my trust'.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.940
And you are right. But remember,
you have all already been

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:26.030
getting used to delegation. We have
started small. We have handed

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:29.940
over tasks to people who have
the skill set, and we started to

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.700
diversify the skill set of our
different team members too.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:40.060
Have faith in them. You cannot
earn trust or build trust if you do

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.100
not allow them the opportunity
to do so.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.800
We're breaking down the language. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.800
Today we're looking at the phrase 'getting used to',

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.000
not to be confused with
'used to' for past habits.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.700
Here, we are adding the phrase 
'to get' or 'to be' in front of it,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:04.600
and it has a similar meaning to
'become familiar with something'.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:10.940
For example, we are getting used
to handing over tasks. We do

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.910
it a little bit, a little bit,
a little bit, until this practice

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:19.490
becomes normal and comfortable
and easier for us. Since Covid,

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.300
many of us have started going
back to the office for work,

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.800
so we are getting used to commuting again.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.070
We've broken down the language.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.880
Now, just because you have faith in your team

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.300
and you are trusting them, doesn't
mean that you can simply check out.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.100
Work.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.100
I'm delegating.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:53.200
Offer support. Have open channels of 
communication and make sure that you clearly

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.400
communicate goals and deadlines
to your team.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.300
Have an open door policy.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.600
And remember, now that you
have gotten used to offloading

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.000
those extra tasks, you should have
more free time to help manage

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.700
your team and their specific needs.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:14.500
Remember guys, there is no such thing as I in team.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.110
I hope that you enjoyed our series
and are practising and improving

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:35.610
your delegation skills at work or
at home. If you haven't already,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.270
please feel free to subscribe
to our channel by clicking on

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.840
the links below. I will
see you next time.

